    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "## Summary\n- retire the external `@asynchronia` plugin invocation from active task schema and bridge wording\n- mark legacy task-artifact directives as `HISTORICAL_NON_AUTHORITATIVE`\n- update the task validator so active Codex artifacts do not require the retired package line and reject it if reintroduced\n- preserve repository-owned task/scope/model checks and bridge continuation safety gates\n\n## Scope\n- control-plane and task-artifact policy only\n- no `AsyncScene/**` or `docs/**` runtime changes\n- no direct main writes\n\n## Validation\n- `python3 -m unittest tools.test_validate_ai_work_pipeline` - PASS (14 tests)\n- `git diff --check` - PASS\n- full `python3 tools/validate_ai_work_pipeline.py` remains blocked by pre-existing incomplete historical task packages on `main`:\n  - `TASK-INFRA-MODEL-PREFLIGHT-E2E-REPAIR-20260717` missing `STATE.md`\n  - `TASK-INFRA-POST-R2-REPOSITORY-MEMORY-CLOSURE-20260719` invalid/incomplete legacy artifacts\n\nStage 7.15 runtime and Safari status are unchanged: 75%, M82 Safari FAIL/unaccepted, M83 not started.\n",
